+`list` and `watch` accept `--owner LABEL` and `--task LABEL` to show only jobs
+whose declared labels match exactly (case-sensitive). Both filters combine with
+AND, and a job without a task never matches `--task`. They work with `--all`,
+`--resources`, `--json`, `watch --once` and `--interval`. Filtering happens
+before the recent-finished window, so up to five matching recently finished jobs
+still appear and every matching active or unverified job stays visible. Scan
+warnings are always reported, because an unreadable record could match. Labels
+must be at most 512 bytes without control characters; an invalid label exits 1
+before anything is listed. Filters are declared labels, not identity or
+authorization. They only narrow the view: they never renew leases, send signals
+or write records, and history collection runs as it does without them.
